{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1779478766,"nonce":"fYodGjfatWnGCN1Xxf2KU8ODzlg=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABDIYWAc69hvsE"},"target":"1e4fe7d9074c0f6b22ac2bd7003a3342cf2f1bb78012a3b2b889be25e38b7c92","message":"## Scope today\n\nPrimary: battery-discharge characterization to LVD trip. Boat is currently at **~25.25 V** (already below yesterday's 26.05 V end-of-session). Combining today's run with 2026-05-19 + 2026-05-21 gives three discharge-curve samples for class-prep battery sizing.\n\nCo-scope: clear two remaining \"Verify before June 4\" items (mercat NTP + AML SVS bag capture) and validate the PR #153 boat-side bag-recording additions; validate the just-merged perception multi-instance fix under in-water load (already deployed on gabby field-side); test costmap delivery to operator rviz over Starlink at extended range.\n\n**Field-side state already on gabby** (to reconcile via PRs post-deployment):\n- `seafloor_echoboat_project11#21` forward-only workaround **reverted** — 4-instance `sea_surface_layer` config restored now that PR [#16](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/pull/16) is merged.\n- `bizzyboat.yaml` vpn `topics_list` — `oak_aft_ffmpeg` **re-added** (was dropped to free Starlink budget; restoring while we see how it fares).\n\n**Field A/B added today** (see comment thread): segmentation FoV widening via 4:3 preview + video on OAK cameras. Switch `video_{width,height}` to `1280×960` and `preview_{width,height}` to `1280×960` in `oak_cameras_launch.py` per-camera; optional `h265_bitrate_kbps` bump 800 → 1066 to preserve bits-per-pixel. Hypothesis: closes ~10° gaps at diagonal seams between adjacent cameras (`unh_marine_perception#10` analysis). Field-test today; revert if framerate drops or bag-disk growth hits a budget.\n\nMission profile: short survey lines close to the pier, low-medium speed, periodic ~200 m extended-range excursions for Starlink load characterization. Stay close to pier once voltage drops \u003c 25 V so an LVD trip doesn't strand the boat.\n\n## Open task issues in scope\n\n- **Battery characterization** *(unfiled — deploy-driven, sized in [#150 topic 5 closure](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/150#issuecomment-4521506548))* — Plot voltage across the boat-on session; produce a 3-sample cross-deployment discharge model.\n- **Verify before June 4** *(from roadmap)*: mercat NTP (`ntpq.exe -pn` captured); AML SVS present in boat-side bag with real (non-zero) sound-speed values.\n- **PR #153 boat-logger additions**: confirm `/bizzy/tide_estimate`, `/bizzy/mllw_offset`, `/bizzy/mhhw_offset` appear in today's bag.\n- [`unh_marine_perception#14`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/14) — PR [#16](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/pull/16) is **MERGED**. Build on gabby + revert `seafloor_echoboat_project11#21`'s forward-only workaround field-side; bench-launch `controller_server` with the 4-instance config to verify no segfault; deploy in-water with full surround coverage.\n- **Costmap over Starlink** — `local_costmap/costmap` is currently configured for the wifi connection only. **Dynamic test via `rqt_udp_bridge`** adds it to the vpn connection at runtime during the extended-range excursion; verify the topic arrives at operator rviz over Starlink.\n- [`unh_echoboats_project11#130`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/130) — quick OTH 4-cam Starlink sanity (capture load profile in-bag; cross-check against the [topic 3 baseline](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/150#issuecomment-4521361343)).\n- [`unh_echoboats_project11#157`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/157) **observe** — fresh launch sequence today; watch whether activation-race retries appear, capture timing if so. Don't actively try to reproduce.\n\n## Hosts active\n\n- **gabby** — boat-side Linux / ROS host (data hub + boat compute)\n- **salmon** — operator station\n- **mercat** — Windows / QINSy host (NTP verify + AML bridge running)\n- **dev** — workspace dev machine (this agent)\n\n## Day plan\n\n### Block 1 — Pre-launch (dock-side, ~45 min)\n\n- [ ] **gabby — confirm field-side state**: 4-instance `sea_surface_layer` config + aft camera back on vpn are already in place per Roland. Verify with `git status` / `git log` on the two repos so the reconciliation PRs at wrap-up have the right SHAs.\n- [ ] **gabby — apply 4:3 OAK A/B test**: edit `bizzyboat_project11/launch/oak_cameras_launch.py` per the comment-thread spec (4 params per camera: `video_{width,height}=1280×960`, `preview_{width,height}=1280×960`; optional bitrate bump). Field-side commit; reconcile at wrap-up. Confirm `ros2 topic hz` on each `oak_*/image_raw/ffmpeg` shows framerate held (~5 Hz). Note bag disk-growth ~+33% on the ffmpeg + raw camera topics.\n- [ ] **Boat-side ROS bring-up**: standard launches. Capture battery voltage at this point. Note: today is the in-water validation of the multi-instance fix — if `controller_server` segfaults on activation, revert to forward-only on the spot and keep the rest of the mission.\n- [ ] **Verify new bag-recording topics**: `ros2 topic echo /bizzy/tide_estimate -n 1`; same for `/bizzy/mllw_offset`, `/bizzy/mhhw_offset`. Confirm they're in `ros2 bag info` on the in-flight bag.\n- [ ] **Mercat NTP verify**: SSH to mercat → `ntpq.exe -pn` → capture to dev log. Expected sync to `time.bizzy.p11.lan` (TM2000B) per [[project_ntp_rutx11]].\n- [ ] **AML SVS dry sanity**: `ros2 topic echo /bizzy/sensors/sound_speed/sound_speed -n 5`. Out-of-water → 0.0 m/s placeholder is expected; check real value once submerged.\n- [ ] **Operator-side bring-up on salmon**: annunciator clean; rviz running with the local_costmap display ready.\n- [ ] **Activation-race observation**: note time of first `Activating controller_server` log message vs first successful `Server controller_server connected with bond` log message. Single-attempt success → activation-race avoided; multiple attempts → captured for [#157](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/157).\n- [ ] **Final pre-launch battery voltage**: recorded.\n\n### Block 2 — In-water mission (run until LVD)\n\n- [ ] **Launch** — record water-entry moment precisely.\n- [ ] **Phase 1 (~15-20 min) — nav-stack health + 4-instance perception + 4:3 A/B eyeballs**: short trackline near the pier; verify costmap populates from all four `sea_surface_layer` instances without segfault under in-water load. Verify chain still produces map_tide and tide_estimate without suppression warnings. **Eyeball the 4:3 A/B**: `rqt_camera_grid` tile aspect should auto-update to 4:3; check that diagonal seam gaps between adjacent cameras have visibly shrunk or closed on the costmap.\n- [ ] **Phase 2 (~30 min) — survey lines**: 50-100 m trackline pattern, low-medium speed. Log battery voltage every 15 min in dev log.\n- [ ] **Phase 3 (~15-20 min) — extended-range / Starlink test + costmap-over-vpn**:\n  - Move to ~200 m range (toward expected WiFi degradation zone).\n  - **Add `local_costmap/costmap` to the vpn topics_list dynamically** via `rqt_udp_bridge` (or equivalent runtime add). Confirm bridging starts.\n  - **Operator rviz**: verify the costmap topic now arrives over Starlink (rviz shows the layer updating). Note update rate + any latency observations.\n  - Cross-check `udp_bridge` per-remote DiagnosticStatus stays healthy under the added load.\n- [ ] **Phase 4 — stay-close drain**: continue surveying near pier. As voltage drops to ~25 V, stay within easy-recovery range. As it drops to ~24 V mean, prepare for LVD trip.\n- [ ] **LVD trip / cutoff**: when LVD trips OR voltage drops below ~23.5 V mean, end mission. Capture cutoff state (voltage, time, last cmd_vel) in dev log.\n\n### Block 3 — Wrap-up (post-recovery)\n\n- [ ] Recovery; final voltage logged.\n- [ ] Pull all bags (boat-side + operator-side) to dev.\n- [ ] **Cross-deployment battery analysis**: extract 2026-05-19, 2026-05-21, today → run `08_battery_voltage.py` variant on combined data; produce 3-sample discharge curve + transient-dip floor estimate. Attach plot to dev log.\n- [ ] AML SVS verify: confirm `/bizzy/sensors/sound_speed/sound_speed` had real (non-zero) values during in-water phase.\n- [ ] Tide_estimate / mllw_offset / mhhw_offset present in today's boat-side bag with sensible values.\n- [ ] Multi-instance `sea_surface_layer` result captured in dev log (no segfault for the full session → durable validation of #14 fix; if it segfaulted at any point, file follow-up issue).\n- [ ] Costmap-over-Starlink result captured (latency + frame rate + operator-rviz subjective experience).\n- [ ] **Reconciliation PRs** (cherry-pick from gabby's field commits):\n  - `seafloor_echoboat_project11` — revert `#21`'s forward-only workaround now that `#14` is fixed and field-validated.\n  - `unh_echoboats_project11` `bizzyboat.yaml` — restore `oak_aft_ffmpeg` to vpn `topics_list`. **Contingent on** today showing it didn't degrade the Starlink path; if it did, drop the line again and document why.\n  - `unh_echoboats_project11` `oak_cameras_launch.py` — 4:3 preview + video A/B. **Contingent on** the A/B holding up (framerate maintained, bag-disk growth acceptable, seam gaps visibly closed). If it didn't, revert and document the finding.\n  - Wrap-up PR on `unh_echoboats_project11` closing this deployment issue (typically includes the bizzyboat.yaml + oak_cameras_launch.py reconciliations as part of the same PR — same pattern as #153).\n  - **Stretch**: if dynamic `local_costmap` on vpn proves valuable during Phase 3, file a small follow-up PR adding it to `bizzyboat.yaml` vpn `topics_list` permanently.\n\n## Tides + weather\n\nTimes in **EDT (UTC−4)**; tide heights in metres relative to MLLW per log convention.\n\n- **Tides — Fort Point NH (NOAA station 8423898, MLLW)**:\n  - L 10:36 EDT — −0.093 m *(before session)*\n  - **H 17:02 EDT — +2.676 m** *(during mission)*\n  - L 22:57 EDT — +0.261 m *(after recovery)*\n\n  Mid-day session = rising tide throughout; Judd Gregg launch unconstrained.\n\n- **Currents — Clark Island NH ACT0731 bin 1** *(populate at deployment start if relevant — mid-rise typical pattern)*.\n\n- **Weather** *(populate at deployment start from NWS Portsmouth point forecast)*.\n\n## Carry-forward cautions\n\n- **[#157](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/157) activation race** — cold-boot today; expect up to 4 retries / ~26 min if the race hits. No mitigation pre-applied (we're observing). If it hangs \u003e 30 s, retry lifecycle bringup manually.\n- **#150 topic 5 transient dips** — at low battery, instantaneous voltage dips can fall ~1.7 V below the mean during thrust bursts. At 24.5 V mean → transients hit 22.8 V. Stay close to the pier when voltage is \u003c 25 V.\n- **#150 topic 6** — if BT action server is \"inactive. Rejecting the goal.\" for \u003e 30 s after launch, retry lifecycle bringup before assuming a deeper failure.\n- **Sidescan / M3 imagery decision** still open *(from roadmap)* — not relevant to today's mission but flag if any decision-input observation surfaces.\n- **No `git pull gitcloud main` to local main** per [[feedback_no_pull_gitcloud_to_local_main]] — field commits reconcile post-deployment via PR.\n- **RC mode-switch at fringe range** — pin controller mode switch to AUTO/GUIDED for autonomous segments.\n\n## Logs\n\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_dev_logs.md` *(create at session start)*\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_gabby_logs.md` *(gabby agent populates)*\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_salmon_logs.md` *(salmon agent populates)*\n- `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_mercat_logs.md` *(mercat agent for NTP capture)*\n\n## Wrap-up checklist\n\n- [ ] Field hosts push logs to gitcloud\n- [ ] Dev pulls field logs into worktree branch\n- [ ] Dev integrates field-agent timeline entries into dev log\n- [ ] Cross-deployment battery analysis attached to dev log\n- [ ] AML SVS verify result in dev log\n- [ ] Mercat NTP verify result in dev log\n- [ ] Tide_estimate / datum topics confirm in dev log\n- [ ] Multi-instance `sea_surface_layer` result captured\n- [ ] Costmap-over-Starlink result captured\n- [ ] 4:3 A/B FoV result captured (seam-gap behavior + framerate + bag-growth)\n- [ ] `seafloor_echoboat_project11` revert PR opened (cherry-pick gabby's field commit)\n- [ ] Open follow-up issues for anything bounded\n- [ ] Update `docs/roadmap.md` with anything deferred / completed\n- [ ] Wrap-up PR closing this deployment issue\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1779477479,"nonce":"nms0s/PLTRB2nes832Z9VSFTWdc=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDIYWAc8AAAAGBbzrEA"},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1779477480,"nonce":"tFmg8MLze3v1SXBE2qXYcEgVrOI=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDIYWAc8AAAAGBbzrQA"},"added":["deployment"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779478273,"nonce":"g7tzkm+KVztpiDEx58dQhNOG3/I=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDYpo6w","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/160#issuecomment-4522141931"},"message":"## Field A/B: segmentation FoV widening (4:3 video + preview)\n\nBackground: prior bag-overlay analysis (case (a) from [`unh_marine_perception#10` multi-camera coverage comment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/10#issuecomment-4504178327)) confirmed the segmentation intrinsics match what the NN actually sees, but the 16:9 → 4:3 center-crop inside `ImageManip` discards ~25% of horizontal lens FoV. At the current 4-camera 90° tiling that leaves ~10° gaps at each diagonal seam (~11% azimuth uncovered).\n\nHypothesis: switching the OAK preview + video streams to 4:3 closes the seam gaps without introducing any projection-side mismatch — `calibrationToCameraInfo(..., 128, 96)` stays correct.\n\n**Config change** — in `bizzyboat_project11/launch/oak_cameras_launch.py`, add to each camera's params:\n\n```python\n'video_width':    1280,\n'video_height':   960,\n'preview_width':  1280,\n'preview_height': 960,\n```\n\nOptional bitrate tune: bump `h265_bitrate_kbps` from 800 → ~1066 per camera to preserve bits-per-pixel (4 cams × 1066 ≈ 4.2 Mbps, comfortably inside both WiFi and Starlink budgets).\n\n**Things to eyeball**:\n- `rqt_camera_grid` should reconfigure tile aspect to 4:3 automatically (target aspect is median of observed image aspects).\n- Bag disk growth ~+33% on `image_raw/ffmpeg` and the raw `camera` topics.\n- Per-camera `ros2 topic hz` to confirm framerate didn't drop under the new size.\n- On a costmap with `sea_surface_layer` active, inter-camera seam gaps should visibly shrink or close.\n\n**Revert**: drop the four params (or comment them out) — defaults are 1280×720.\n\nCaveat not yet field-tested: with the unified `dai::node::Camera`, I'm not 100% certain `setPreviewSize` and `setSize` deliver truly independent ISP-scaled streams when their aspect ratios differ. Flipping video + preview together (both 4:3) sidesteps the question.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}